        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 65-year-old female patient, admitted on 25/06/2014 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, clinical examination revealed significant dyspnoea, prolonged expiration, and reduced oxygen saturation. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory changes. Spirometry confirmed severe obstructive ventilatory impairment. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Vital signs were monitored continuously. Under treatment, her condition improved satisfactorily. Prior to discharge, patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided. Please arrange early follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Discharge medication includes inhaled bronchodilators and a tapering course of oral corticosteroids. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>"
            },
